 Will prevent every job tagged as ``daily-tasks`` from running again.
 
 
+Pause and resume jobs by tag
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+To temporarily stop a group of jobs (e.g. during a maintenance window)
+without cancelling them, use ``schedule.pause(tag)``. Paused jobs are skipped
+by ``run_pending()`` until ``schedule.resume(tag)`` is called.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    schedule.every().hour.do(sync_data).tag('db')
+
+    schedule.pause('db')   # sync_data is skipped
+    schedule.resume('db')  # sync_data is eligible to run again
+
+A job that became due while paused runs once on the next ``run_pending()``
+after it is resumed. ``run_all()`` ignores pausing.
+
+
